    "statement": "In the stabilizer argument for a degree-four cover, a point x of Gamma that is unramified for gamma need not lie in gamma^{-1}(P^1 minus branch locus), since another point of its fibre may be ramified; 'a deck transformation of the connected etale part fixing a point is the identity' therefore does not apply literally. The correct and equally short argument is that id and sigma are two sections of pr_1: C x_{P^1} C -> C, which is etale at (x,x) because gamma is unramified at x, so they agree on a neighbourhood of x and hence on all of the connected reduced C. Reusable write-up correction for any stabilizer/rigidity clause in this campaign that fixes an unramified marked point.",
